## 1. Process Initialization & Self-Correction Flow

When `pnpm run dev` kicks off `jarvis.ts`, the `SelfHealingManager` manages the Python processes silently.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant OS as Operating System
    participant SHM as SelfHealingManager
    participant NB as NodeBridge (WS: 9000)
    participant WW as wakeWords.py
    participant STT as stt.py (Whisper)
    participant TTS as tts.py (EdgeTTS)

    %% Startup
    OS->>SHM: Start JARVIS (jarvis.ts)
    SHM->>NB: Start WebSocket Server
    SHM->>WW: spawn() as Child Process
    SHM->>STT: spawn() as Child Process
    SHM->>TTS: spawn() as Child Process

    %% Connection Handshake
    WW->>NB: Connect as "wakeword" & Send READY
    TTS->>NB: Connect as "tts" & Send READY
    STT->>STT: Load Whisper Model (Background Thread)
    STT->>NB: Connect WS (Awaiting Model)
    STT->>NB: Model Loaded -> Send READY as "stt"
    NB->>TTS: Flush Boot "JARVIS online" Greeting
```

> [!TIP]
> Notice the **Background Threading** behavior in `stt.py`. Since Whisper takes ~10 seconds to load, moving this to a background thread allows STT to connect immediately without being marked as "Crashed" or timing out.

